				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 4.5d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"What is the impact of an electric blast furnace melting items at a certain temperature? Each electric blast furnace recipe has a specific base temperature. For example, aluminum is smelted at 1700K. If the temperature is not high enough, the recipe will not be executed. If the temperature is high enough, the time consumption will be reduced."
				""
				"The temperature mainly depends on the coil grade used, but beyond that there is a 100K increase in temperature for each voltage grade starting from HV. This means that at some point it is possible to use a lower stage coil with a high enough voltage to run certain recipes that would appear to only be possible with a higher stage coil."
			]
			icon: "kubejs:uruium_coil_block"
			id: "2205C5F410B9C4DB"
			rewards: [{
				exclude_from_claim_all: true
				id: "502F72B2B473E1F5"
				table_id: 6225023274141477362L
				type: "random"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "50F636D9BF4F6025"
				title: "Coil"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 0.5d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Multi-block structures are checked to see if they have sufficient power before working."
				""
				"The power consumed by multiple blocks is the sum of all energy bins."
				""
				"For example, electricity requires a power input of at least 120EU/t to run its recipe. This can be achieved through two LV energy bins. Each bin requires 2 amps of LV, so a total of 4 amps of LV are needed to achieve a maximum power of 128EU/t. That is,&bdouble warehouse boost &r."
				"This allows low voltage levels to process high voltage level recipes. Note that this can only be achieved in adjacent voltages, that is,&6can only boost&ronce, and two&renergy bins&band&rmust be used."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_energy_input_hatch"
			id: "0BADECF30AC0BAC4"
			rewards: [{
				exclude_from_claim_all: true
				id: "0E4F322748AB8F3B"
				table_id: 6225023274141477362L
				type: "random"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "23E71635D04A5A77"
				title: "powered by"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: -3.5d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"This is the key to the input and output of multi-block structures. More advanced buses/bins/assemblies will provide more space."
				""
				"The bus/bin/assembly also comes with&dautomatic input and output&rfunctions, which can be controlled by switches."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_input_bus"
			id: "5DB8BE71B3733C36"
			rewards: [{
				exclude_from_claim_all: true
				id: "3100FD76AEA9BF1D"
				table_id: 6225023274141477362L
				type: "random"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "35761A42191E549C"
				title: "bus/bin"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: -1.5d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"When 16 LV machines are run simultaneously, the power is equal to that of one HV machine, but the speed is four times that of one HV machine. This is because the 16 LV machines did not suffer losses caused by lossy overclocking. causing it to do it faster at a lower speed."
				""
				"The parallelism of multi-block structures is a similar concept. Simply put, parallelism is an alternative form of lossless overclocking."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Sub-tick parallelism (1toc) is a mechanism that is triggered when some multi-block structures take less than 1 game tick to process a single recipe."
				""
				"All single block machines and cross-recipe parallel machines will not trigger 1toc."
				""
				"Example 1: When a multi-block machine with voltage levelLuVtakes exactly 1 game tick to process recipes with voltage level IV, the machine will process 2 recipes per game tick. If the voltage level of the machine is one level higher (reachingZPMlevel), it will process 4 recipes per game tick; if the machine has a lossless overclocking mechanism (such as a large chemical reactor), it will process 4 recipes per game tick respectively atLuVand LuV.ZPMlevel processes 4 and 16 recipes in parallel."
				""
				"Example 2: For a recipe that takes 3 game ticks and the recipe is lossless overclocking (the time taken for each overclocking level is reduced to 1/4 of the original, and the total energy consumption remains unchanged), after one level of overclocking, 4 recipes will be processed at the same time, but the time is still 3 game ticks."
				""
				"In fact, there is a difference between \"lossy 1toc\" and \"lossless 1toc\". The above example is only for reference."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Cross-recipe parallelism is a mechanism exclusive to some multi-block machines, which allows the machine to execute multiple different recipes in the same machine mode at the same time."
				""
				"Correspondingly, the lower limit of recipe time for all machines with cross-recipe parallelism is 1 second."
				""
				"Example: The Holy Separator can make silver rods and iron rods at the same time, but cannot centrifuge air and make iron rods at the same time."
				""
				"\"Threads\" is a unique attribute of machines with cross-recipe parallelism (all have 64 threads). The total parallel number of a cross-recipe parallel machine is the number of threads multiplied by the parallel number of the machine itself. The number of threads represents the maximum number of recipes that the total parallel number can be allocated to. Note: The cross-recipe parallel machine will try its best to allocate all total parallelism to a recipe."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:iv_parallel_hatch"
			id: "6F503441C24ABD5B"
			rewards: [{
				exclude_from_claim_all: true
				id: "0E0EC544E98C754A"
				table_id: 6225023274141477362L
				type: "random"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "6B1CC517916931AB"
				title: "parallel"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: 6.5d
			y: -8.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
